From fb3cf675dd689b72b56f97c0682fa21257267996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0racl-lab <360770237+0racl-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 11:15:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add read_evm_tx service (interface 8)

One finalized EVM transaction: block number, block hash, block timestamp,
position, sender, recipient, native value, nonce, type, status and log
count. The sibling of read_evm_log: that returns what a transaction
emitted, this returns when and by whom, so a contract can accept a token
transfer only if it was made after a given moment.

Per endpoint the transaction, receipt and block (fetched by the hash the
receipt names) must tell one consistent story; every endpoint must agree
byte-for-byte and report the block finalized, otherwise the service
abstains. A reverted transaction is a final result (status 0), not "not
finalized". Stdlib-only Python with a mock node and a 33-check selftest.
Node config, docker-compose and example_env register the slot (port 9010)
and reuse EVM_RPC_URLS_<chainId>.
Requires the matching qubic/core interface (EvmTxRead.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QHXGjDwxBARUytE2smA8oq
